=\"questionWidget-spinnerFrame\"><div class=\"questionWidget-spinner\" style=\"display: block;\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-correctIncorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/correct-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-correctText\">Correct</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>Recall that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>A set is <em>open</em> if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>A set is <em>closed</em> if it contains <strong>all</strong> of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Let's examine our sets in turn.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The first set is <em>open</em> since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The second set is <em>closed</em> since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The third set is <em>closed</em> since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"</p>\n</div></div>",
